Note: lspy is an independent, from-scratch command-line implementation of the
LocalSend protocol written in Python, using the standard library only. It
implements the same HTTP endpoints and discovery mechanism described by the
public LocalSend protocol documentation in order to interoperate with official
clients. It does not copy, link against, or modify the source code of the
official LocalSend app.

Sibling implementations maintained by the same author:
  - OldSend   (https://github.com/styisme/oldsend)
  - WatchSend (https://github.com/styisme/watchsend)

Those projects share protocol ideas with lspy but no code; lspy is not a fork
of either of them.

